{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7847","id":5216139455,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNuf4vw","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7847","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7847.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7847.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7847","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7847/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7847/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7847/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/884ad6fbf5b121069f7f01b732e05c365529be39","number":7847,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"mcpx v2: daemon picker tool — closest equivalent of the TUI select (#2841 item 3)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nImplements **#1858 SET-REMAINDER item (3)** under #2841: the mcpx OpenCode v2 daemon picker — as the closest supported equivalent of the requested TUI `select()`, because the pinned v2 surface cannot support a true TUI select.\n\n## Deviation evidence (pinned API)\n\nVerified 2026-11-08 against the pinned opencode fork (`~/git/opencode` at `ededbacbfd`, `@opencode/plugin` version **2.0.30**):\n\n- `packages/plugin/src/promise/plugin.ts` — the setup `Context` has a fixed domain list (agent, aisdk, command, credential, event, integration, mcp, messaging, model, generate, permission, plugin, provider, reference, rpc, session, shell, skill, storage, tool, vcs, websearch, worktree). There is **no ui/tui/question domain**, and no select/dialog/prompt method on any domain a server plugin receives. (The `question` tool is a built-in model tool with `codemode: false`, not a plugin surface.)\n- The v1 picker (`mcpx-tui.tsx`) works only because v1 has a separate TUI plugin realm (`@opencode-ai/plugin/tui`, `DialogSelect`). The v2 module contract (`{ id, setup }` / `{ id, effect }`) has no TUI counterpart in the pin.\n\nThis deviation is also recorded on #2841 and #1858, as item (3) requires.\n\n## The equivalent: `mcpx_daemon_pick`\n\n- **No index** → renders the picker menu: ranked candidates, the in-use daemon marked (DialogSelect's `current`), each option carrying the config path that actually distinguishes daemons plus started/servers/sessions/version detail — the v1 DialogSelect options, as tool output.\n- **With an index** → asserts `mcpx_daemon_select` through the permission domain with the same payload `daemon_select` sends (the one interactive channel v2 server plugins have), and only a confirmed selection reaches the `ctx.storage`-backed apply (`remember.ts`), at the requested scope.\n- **Cancellation is a picker outcome, not an error:** a rejected assert applies nothing and reports the choice unchanged. Invalid indexes, no candidates, picker errors, and a missing permission domain likewise never change the selected daemon.\n\n`picker.ts` holds the host-free core (`buildPickerOptions`, `renderPickerMenu`, `runPickerSelection`); `tools.ts` wires it to discovery/`applyChoice`; `daemon_select` is unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `picker.test.ts` — menu options/current marking; the selection oracle is state: apply runs only after a successful assert, with exactly the picked target + scope; cancellation / invalid index / no permission domain / no candidates all leave apply uncalled.\n- `tools.test.ts` — registration gains `mcpx_daemon_pick`; menu render at tool level; a confirmed pick **persists through stub ctx.storage** (`daemon:/work` record holds the picked target); a cancelled pick leaves storage empty and fires no target change.\n- `bun test plugin/opencode/v2/` — **73 pass, 0 fail** (baseline on main: 61 pass).\n\n## Scope\n\nItem (3) only. Item (5) v1 retirement is **not** included — it remains sequenced after item (3) lands or is waived. Items (1), (2), (4) already landed (#5122/#5170, #3018, #4997).\n\nRefs #2841, #1858. Queue task 13615 (lane code-h).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796771762&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7847&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7847&signature=136c52f0da0c30aba00b1981355e7567378b878af72a63642bd307f7f1c2a5b0\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7847?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T23:15:58Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T23:48:16Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T23:48:14Z","merged_at":"2026-11-08T23:48:14Z","merge_commit_sha":"62e12a01755576a42fc6dc640f7f2858dc246b90","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_teams":[{"id":7767549,"node_id":"T_kwDOAZNvF84AdoX9","url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549","members_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/members{/member}","name":"codeowners","description":"Team Discussions: developing-today/code","permission":"pull","privacy":